package report

// cloudInstruction is reasonedInstruction for the checks of a cloud benchmark, keyed by Prowler's
// check name. The row takes the instruction as its title and Prowler's sentence about the resource
// beneath it. Prowler titles a check by the state it wants, "EBS default encryption is enabled",
// which beside a failed check reads as a pass, so its title is never a row's.
//
// Each sentence holds for every resource the check fails, on every branch of the check that fails
// one: read the check's code and the helpers it calls, not its title. Where the cloud allows only one
// fix, the sentence names it, and says what becomes of the resource it replaces: an RDS instance's
// storage cannot be encrypted in place, and the unencrypted instance fails until it is gone. A check
// that can flag something deliberate leaves room with an "unless".
//
// A name two clouds share, kms_key_not_publicly_accessible, has one sentence true on both, since the
// rule does not say which cloud it ran on. A check Prowler reports only as MANUAL has no entry, and
// neither does one outside the default frameworks: its row keeps the check's name as its title, over
// Prowler's sentence.
